{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL7mv4SAidtggVPGwYmD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LtgLmbsmfmHEfLYUyyocfo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nsub(\"Review feedback is added by the review-feedback loop. The agent edits\",\"In a review round, `.ard-input/<issue#>/review-feedback.md` (the untrusted header, the round, the committed role files of the reviewers that asked for changes and the pull request comments of people, cut at 64 KiB), and the reviewer role files and logs on the branch are untrusted inputs too. The agent edits\")\nsub(\"and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`, `issue.md`, the triage role files and logs. It writes\",\"and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`, `issue.md`, the triage role files and logs, in a review round `review-feedback.md` and the reviewer role files and logs. It writes\")\ni=s.index(\"**Review feedback loops back here.**\"); j=s.index(\"**The merger takes it from here.**\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"**Review feedback loops back here.** The `reviewfix` loop (#41) starts a round when every requested reviewer has finished and at least one ended `ard:review:<role>:changes`, backed by that role's close-out record (a label alone does not count). It records a `review_round` event in `_controller.db` (counted when requested, ordered by event ID, local to that database) and removes `ard:worker:<role>:done` from the issue, so the worker loop claims it again. The worker fixes on the same branch and reads `review-feedback.md`. When the fix lands with code changes, every requested reviewer runs again at the new head (their `:done` and `:changes` labels come off), because merge-gating approvals must cover the merged head. A round that changes no code, or one that would pass `max_review_rounds` (default 3), posts one comment and adds `ard:needs-human` on the issue; it is not repeated on the same head after a person removes the label. Merger conflict and rebase rounds are a follow-up that will use the same round API (`reviewfix.RequestRound`); until then a conflict, like a red required check, goes to `ard:needs-human`.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nsub(\"In round 2 and later it also gets its previous findings and must say which are resolved (review feedback loop).\",\"In a later round it also gets `.ard-input/<issue#>/previous-review.md`, its own earlier report, read from the pinned head, and says which findings are resolved.\")\nsub(\"and #41 will turn this into a rebase round that counts toward `max_review_rounds`\",\"and a follow-up to #41 will turn this into a rebase round (`reviewfix.RequestRound`) that counts toward `max_review_rounds`\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; gofmt -l internal; make lint test 2>&1 | grep -v \"redact.log\" | tail -25"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4518,"cache_read_input_tokens":112984,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4518},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cdc0f494-ef68-48c0-8855-e4e66ae11845","uuid":"ce492609-1baf-44b8-aa73-039b0f1e0395","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:44:34.134Z","request_id":"req_011ChL7mutkpySQzRemz5Ynh"}
