{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL7rx3t7NzEQbTaP8SHG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `reviewfix` loop is in. A worker PR with a proven `:changes` verdict now goes back to its worker, and the issue goes to `ard:needs-human` at `max_review_rounds` or when a round changes no code. `make lint test` passes.\n\n- **Done-when test:** it is the two end-to-end tests in `internal/servecmd/reviewfix_e2e_test.go`. One goes changes → fix → approve and marks the PR ready. The other stops at the cap with one comment and `ard:needs-human`. Both simulate the worker rather than running the worker loop, as the plan says.\n- **Layout line:** the line for `CLAUDE.md` is in the PR body for a maintainer to add.\n\nChanges beyond what the plan listed:\n- I moved the worker round-trip test in `internal/prgate` into a new external test file. Without that, `prgate` tests import `worker`, which now imports `reviewfix`, which imports `prgate`, and that is an import cycle.\n- The reviewer test harness gained a `FileAt` stub so the previous-review test can feed it a file.\n- The loop-count and error-text assertions in the `servecmd` tests are updated for the new loop.\n\nTwo gaps in the tests:\n- **Same-second claim row:** I did not add a separate row for a worker claim in the same second as the `requested` event. The loop orders events by ID, so every row already depends on that.\n- **Dry-run log lines:** the dry-run row checks that no events and no writes happen, but not the log lines.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/41/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":119959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":932},"output_tokens":521,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics